{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Java code to Python 3 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following Java 8 code to Python 3 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original Java 8 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\nimport java.io.PrintWriter;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner in = new Scanner(System.in);\n        PrintWriter out = new PrintWriter(System.out);\n        solve(in, out);\n        out.close();\n    }\n\n    static void solve(Scanner in, PrintWriter out) {\n        int n = in.nextInt();\n        if (n > 11) {\n            out.println(0);\n            return;\n        }\n        ArrayList<Point> arr = new ArrayList<>();\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n            arr.add(new Point(in.nextInt(), in.nextInt(), in.nextInt(), in.nextInt(), in.nextInt()));\n        }\n        TreeSet<Integer> good = new TreeSet<>();\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n            Point p = arr.get(i);\n            boolean ok = true;\n            for (int j = 0; j < n && ok; j++) {\n                for (int k = 0; k < n && ok; k++) {\n                    if (i != j && i != k && j != k) {\n                        Point v1 = sub(arr.get(j), p);\n                        Point v2 = sub(arr.get(k), p);\n                        if (angle(v1, v2)) {\n                            ok = false;\n                        }\n                    }\n                }\n            }\n            if (ok) {\n                good.add(i + 1);\n            }\n        }\n        if (good.size() == 0) {\n            out.println(0);\n        } else {\n            out.println(good.size());\n            for (int idx : good) {\n                out.println(idx);\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    static Point sub(Point a, Point b) {\n        return new Point(a.v - b.v, a.w - b.w, a.x - b.x, a.y - b.y, a.z - b.z);\n    }\n\n    static boolean angle(Point a, Point b) {\n        double amag = a.mag();\n        double bmag = b.mag();\n        int dot = a.v * b.v + a.w * b.w + a.x * b.x + a.y * b.y + a.z * b.z;\n        double ang = Math.toDegrees(Math.acos(dot / (amag * bmag)));\n        return ang < 90;\n    }\n\n    static class Point {\n        int v, w, x, y, z;\n        Point(int v, int w, int x, int y, int z) {\n            this.v = v; this.w = w; this.x = x; this.y = y; this.z = z;\n        }\n        double mag() {\n            return Math.sqrt(v * v + w * w + x * x + y * y + z * z);\n        }\n    }\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport sys\nimport math\n\nclass Point:\n    def __init__(self, v, w, x, y, z):\n        self.v = v\n        self.w = w\n        self.x = x\n        self.y = y\n        self.z = z\n\n    def mag(self):\n        return math.sqrt(self.v * self.v + self.w * self.w + self.x * self.x + self.y * self.y + self.z * self.z)\n\ndef sub(a, b):\n    return Point(a.v - b.v, a.w - b.w, a.x - b.x, a.y - b.y, a.z - b.z)\n\ndef angle(a, b):\n    amag = a.mag()\n    bmag = b.mag()\n    dot = a.v * b.v + a.w * b.w + a.x * b.x + a.y * b.y + a.z * b.z\n    cos_val = dot / (amag * bmag)\n    # Clamp to avoid domain errors due to floating point\n    cos_val = max(-1.0, min(1.0, cos_val))\n    ang = math.degrees(math.acos(cos_val))\n    return ang < 90\n\ndef solve():\n    data = sys.stdin.read().strip().split()\n    if not data:\n        return\n    it = iter(data)\n    n = int(next(it))\n    if n > 11:\n        print(0)\n        return\n    arr = []\n    for _ in range(n):\n        v = int(next(it))\n        w = int(next(it))\n        x = int(next(it))\n        y = int(next(it))\n        z = int(next(it))\n        arr.append(Point(v, w, x, y, z))\n    good = []\n    for i in range(n):\n        p = arr[i]\n        ok = True\n        for j in range(n):\n            if not ok:\n                break\n            for k in range(n):\n                if not ok:\n                    break\n                if i != j and i != k and j != k:\n                    v1 = sub(arr[j], p)\n                    v2 = sub(arr[k], p)\n                    if angle(v1, v2):\n                        ok = False\n        if ok:\n            good.append(i + 1)\n    if not good:\n        print(0)\n    else:\n        print(len(good))\n        for idx in good:\n            print(idx)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    solve()\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n1.0\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-1.0728830375228426e-06, 0.0, 0.0, -2.2172682292875834e-05, -5.483612312673358e-06, -0.0024756519123911858, -0.0007400158210657537, -6.198863957251888e-06, 0.0, -0.0001292145170737058, -0.1002069041132927, 0.0, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -3.576278118089249e-07, -0.00015853578224778175, -1.1920928244535389e-07, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, -4.768360213347478e-06, -0.00033945043105632067, 0.0, -2.3841855067985307e-07, 0.0, -3.576278118089249e-07, 0.0, -2.3841855067985307e-07, 0.0, -3.814689989667386e-06, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, -4.5536911784438416e-05, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -7.152555099310121e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, 0.0, 0.0, -2.3841855067985307e-07, 0.0, 0.0, -2.3841855067985307e-07, 0.0, 0.0, -1.1920928244535389e-0